WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
Why can their fingers

2
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.433
make you laugh,

3
00:00:02.433 --> 00:00:03.833
but yours usually can't?

4
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Both touch your skin.

5
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.833
One important clue

6
00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:07.633
is prediction.

7
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.467
When you move your hand,

8
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.467
your nervous system

9
00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.767
can anticipate the touch

10
00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:12.767
it will produce.

11
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.400
That touch can feel weaker.

12
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.833
Scientists call this

13
00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:17.767
sensory attenuation.

14
00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:19.000
In experiments,

15
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:19.967
self-produced touch

16
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:21.400
felt less ticklish

17
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.300
than matching external touch.

18
00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:24.600
Adding a delay

19
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.033
to a robotic self-touch

20
00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.833
made it feel more ticklish.

21
00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:29.333
But those experiments

22
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:30.633
used light touch,

23
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:32.400
not full-on tickle laughter.

24
00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.300
You can give yourself

25
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.033
a light, tickly sensation.

26
00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:36.933
Laughter-inducing tickling

27
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:38.667
is harder to explain,

28
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:39.967
and people differ.

29
00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.167
Prediction is an important clue,

30
00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.733
not the whole answer.

31
00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:45.200
Your nervous system

32
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.733
doesn't just receive touch.

33
00:00:46.733 --> 00:00:48.667
It can anticipate your own.
